WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:05.430
Dr. Gears was having another boring day at
the SCP Foundation - and that was exactly

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:06.999
how he liked it.

00:00:06.999 --> 00:00:13.110
He’d treated himself to a cup of decaf black
coffee - no cream, no sugar - a single plain

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:14.780
donut, and an apple.

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:18.100
The breakfast of champions, to him at least.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:23.450
His duties today were ones he’d overseen
so many times before: Watching his ever-rotating

00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:29.320
legion of subordinates shove various items
into SCP-914, the Clockworks, just to see

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:31.310
what on earth would happen.

00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:35.940
This machine had the ability to transmute
matter in a variety of fashions, depending

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:43.070
on the input selection, whether Rough, Course,
One To One, Fine, or even Very Fine.

00:00:43.070 --> 00:00:48.699
They’d tested everything - from Dr. Gears’
watch to a chimp, which, as we all know, resulted

00:00:48.699 --> 00:00:52.350
in the beloved hyper-intelligent chimp scientist,
Dr. Bobo.

00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:58.609
There were, in fact, such extensive testing
records for SCP-914 that Dr. Gears had started

00:00:58.609 --> 00:01:02.410
taking an uncharacteristic hands-off approach
to testing.

00:01:02.410 --> 00:01:06.510
As long as the researchers working under him
were reasonably sure that the results of their

00:01:06.510 --> 00:01:11.700
testing wouldn’t result in a containment
breach, a fundamental alteration of consensus

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:16.470
reality, or some massive loss of life, they
could just go ahead with whatever dumb little

00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:18.280
experiment their heart desired.

00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:23.640
This, however, would turn out to be a way
longer leash than Dr. Gears ever should have

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:27.780
given to the kinds of weirdos who work at
the SCP Foundation.

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:33.380
There had been certain, let’s say, incidents
in the past that have proved members of the

00:01:33.380 --> 00:01:38.860
SCP Foundation aren’t above using anomalies
inappropriately for their own personal enjoyment.

00:01:38.860 --> 00:01:45.270
There was, of course, the incident with SCP-662,
the Butler’s Hand Bell, and the supernatural

00:01:45.270 --> 00:01:47.500
Butler it summons, Mr. Deeds.

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:53.300
During the early stages of testing, Dr. Mirth,
under the guise of experimentation, made Mr.

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:58.710
Deeds make him tea, wash his car, cut his
hair, and even do his laundry.

00:01:58.710 --> 00:02:03.490
Dr. Mirth was given a stern talking to by
the O5 Council for this abuse of power.

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:05.410
Good job, O5 Council.

00:02:05.410 --> 00:02:08.679
It’s not like you ever use anomalies for
your own benefit.

00:02:08.679 --> 00:02:09.679
Uhhh...

00:02:09.679 --> 00:02:13.650
Let’s move on, nothing to see here, folks.

00:02:13.650 --> 00:02:18.069
Speaking of people working for the Foundation
using anomalies inappropriately, who could

00:02:18.069 --> 00:02:24.470
forget the extremely uncomfortable incident
involving SCP-137, A Real Toy.

00:02:24.470 --> 00:02:29.670
This anomaly has the ability to become a real-life
version of any toy brought into its vicinity,

00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:33.360
from the Masters of the Universe to Barbie
in her Dream House.

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:38.170
But one researcher was hiding a horrifying
secret: He was...

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:39.170
A Brony.

00:02:39.170 --> 00:02:43.730
And that’s why he sneaked a Twilight Sparkle
toy into the testing chamber, so he could

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:48.999
have a conversation with his favorite My Little
Pony Character, which all in attendance agreed

00:02:48.999 --> 00:02:53.319
just had incredibly rancid vibes through and
through.

00:02:53.319 --> 00:02:58.010
And that brings us back to today: Dr. Gears
deciding to let his subordinate researchers

00:02:58.010 --> 00:03:02.720
throw pretty much anything into the Clockworks
as long as it was unlikely to cause physical

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:03.720
harm.

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:09.469
And leaving this metaphorical door open allowed
people like Dr. Segal to step through.

00:03:09.469 --> 00:03:13.930
You see, while Dr. Segal was considered by
most to be an incredibly diligent and hard-working

00:03:13.930 --> 00:03:20.540
junior researcher, he did have one vice in
his downtime: He was a card-carrying Furry.

00:03:20.540 --> 00:03:24.640
And we’re not just talking about a guy who
watched Disney’s Zootopia a few too many

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:33.450
times, he had his own fursona - a Wolf, if
you were curious - he attended cons for fellow

00:03:33.450 --> 00:03:39.989
furries semi-frequently and even had his own
expensive, custom, high-end fur suit.

00:03:39.989 --> 00:03:48.269
As such, there was one SCP he found particularly
interesting: SCP-1471, also known as MalO

00:03:48.269 --> 00:03:54.769
ver1.O.O, an anomalous mobile app with some
extremely strange properties.

00:03:54.769 --> 00:04:00.010
If you access it on an App Store of your choice,
you’ll encounter an image of a strange,

00:04:00.010 --> 00:04:04.480
skull-headed canine creature, with the following
iconic description:

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:06.469
MalO
ver1.O.O

00:04:06.469 --> 00:04:08.150
FREE!

00:04:08.150 --> 00:04:10.629
Reviews (O)
Description:

00:04:10.629 --> 00:04:14.180
Never settle for those awkward feelings of
being alone ever again.

00:04:14.180 --> 00:04:19.680
MalO is an exciting and interactive experience
that will keep you engaged and intrigued.

00:04:19.680 --> 00:04:25.930
The anxiety of social situations can be nerve-racking,
but after just a few hours of MalO you will

00:04:25.930 --> 00:04:29.330
soon forget all about those painful emotions
of disappointment.

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:34.960
Be part of the new craze that is quickly becoming
the next social substitute.

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:39.770
Remember, the more you participate, the more
MalO will engage you.

00:04:39.770 --> 00:04:42.520
Your experience is completely up to you.

00:04:42.520 --> 00:04:44.169
Absolutely NO ADS.

00:04:44.169 --> 00:04:45.169
Enjoy!

00:04:45.169 --> 00:04:50.430
Dr. Segal was certainly eager to forget all
his painful emotions of disappointment and

00:04:50.430 --> 00:04:53.199
embrace the new social substitute.

00:04:53.199 --> 00:04:57.710
But he’d read all the documents and seen
all the pictures on the file: Those who download

00:04:57.710 --> 00:05:05.009
the MalO app will be texted a series of photos,
becoming closer to home over time, both literally

00:05:05.009 --> 00:05:11.210
and figuratively, which show the strange creature
known as MalO getting closer and closer.

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:13.740
For some, this would be a complete nightmare.

00:05:13.740 --> 00:05:17.870
For those inclined in the direction of Dr.
Segal, it would be a dream come true.

00:05:17.870 --> 00:05:21.970
There was only one issue: They were just pictures.

00:05:21.970 --> 00:05:27.370
But Dr. Segal didn’t get a job at the SCP
Foundation by having a lack of intelligence.

00:05:27.370 --> 00:05:32.139
He’d very quickly figured out a potential
solution to the digital barrier between him

00:05:32.139 --> 00:05:37.669
and his canid crush: He’d buy a burner phone,
download the MalO app onto it, and put the

00:05:37.669 --> 00:05:41.580
resulting infected device directly into the
Clockworks.

00:05:41.580 --> 00:05:46.099
It was one of the best ideas he’d ever had,
in his own humble opinion.

00:05:46.099 --> 00:05:50.330
But of course, it would all be about selecting
the right setting.

00:05:50.330 --> 00:05:54.330
On Rough, the most likely result would be
the phone itself just being transformed into

00:05:54.330 --> 00:05:59.509
a pile of broken glass, metal, and a variety
of conflict minerals reduced to dust.

00:05:59.509 --> 00:06:03.530
On Coarse, the result would likely be the
metal chassis of the phone, the front glass

00:06:03.530 --> 00:06:07.169
panel, and a neatly arranged interior gutted
from within.

00:06:07.169 --> 00:06:11.979
On 1:1, considering he’d bought a slightly
older, cheaper model of Samsung Smart Phone,

00:06:11.979 --> 00:06:15.230
he’d probably just get the MalO app on an
iPhone.

00:06:15.230 --> 00:06:21.241
And on Fine, perhaps the best he could hope
for was getting MalO Ver 2.O.O, which would

00:06:21.241 --> 00:06:25.689
maybe have some minor improvement like the
pictures appearing twice as fast as they would

00:06:25.689 --> 00:06:27.780
with the normal app experience.

00:06:27.780 --> 00:06:33.539
Dr. Segal knew that the only option that could
potentially bring MalO into the real world

00:06:33.539 --> 00:06:39.169
was the highly unpredictable Very Fine option,
which would either produce the desired result

00:06:39.169 --> 00:06:42.379
or cause something utterly horrifying to happen.

00:06:42.379 --> 00:06:46.560
But at the end of the day, Dr. Segal thought
to himself, isn’t anything worth having

00:06:46.560 --> 00:06:49.020
also worth incurring a little risk?

00:06:49.020 --> 00:06:52.090
Who dares, wins, after all, right?

00:06:52.090 --> 00:06:56.460
He downloaded the fateful app and made his
way into the testing area for SCP-914.

00:06:56.460 --> 00:07:02.009
He’d booked the slot, so it was all official,
but he still felt his heart racing as he put

00:07:02.009 --> 00:07:04.759
the infected phone into the Input chamber.

00:07:04.759 --> 00:07:10.129
He set the control panel to Very Fine, exactly
as planned, and activated the machine.

00:07:10.129 --> 00:07:15.180
Cogs twisted and churned, engines rumbled
and sputtered, pipes wriggled and hissed.

00:07:15.180 --> 00:07:17.889
It was clear that something was going on here.

00:07:17.889 --> 00:07:22.110
When the process was complete and the Output
chamber opened with a billowing carpet of

00:07:22.110 --> 00:07:26.000
steam, Dr. Segal could barely contain his
excitement.

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:30.479
He hoped that MalO would come strolling out
of the smoke like Darth Vader in Star Wars:

00:07:30.479 --> 00:07:36.469
A New Hope, so you can only imagine his extreme
disappointment when the chamber was completely

00:07:36.469 --> 00:07:37.469
empty.

00:07:37.469 --> 00:07:38.469
It didn’t make sense.

00:07:38.469 --> 00:07:40.199
He’d thought everything through.

00:07:40.199 --> 00:07:43.889
How could the result possibly be so anti-climatic?

00:07:43.889 --> 00:07:48.249
This had gone from one of the most exciting
days of his life to the most depressing.

00:07:48.249 --> 00:07:53.319
Dr. Segal sighed and decided to call it quits,
heading out of the test chamber, having no

00:07:53.319 --> 00:07:57.259
idea what he’d just unleashed onto the Foundation.

00:07:57.259 --> 00:08:02.349
Across the site, Dr. Alto Clef, one of the
Foundation’s more infamous researchers,

00:08:02.349 --> 00:08:05.340
was polishing his favorite shotgun in his
office.

00:08:05.340 --> 00:08:10.270
He was whistling a cheerful tune to himself,
just loving life, when he heard some strange

00:08:10.270 --> 00:08:11.669
rustling by the door.

00:08:11.669 --> 00:08:15.340
He turned around on his swivel chair, just
to make sure it wasn’t Dr. Bright putting

00:08:15.340 --> 00:08:20.120
another bucket of battery acid on top of his
door as a “fun, harmless prank.”

00:08:20.120 --> 00:08:28.860
Instead, he was shocked to see MalO - an actual,
physical MalO - standing in his doorway, grinning.

00:08:28.860 --> 00:08:31.689
For a moment, Clef was too shocked to even
react.

00:08:31.689 --> 00:08:33.840
This didn’t make any kind of sense.

00:08:33.840 --> 00:08:39.310
But when MalO gave him a cheeky wink, he immediately
loaded his shotgun and fired, blowing away

00:08:39.310 --> 00:08:41.089
a chunk of his own doorway.

00:08:41.089 --> 00:08:46.350
But sadly for him, by that time, MalO had
already darted away, intent on causing mischief

00:08:46.350 --> 00:08:49.140
elsewhere, its favorite pastime.

00:08:49.140 --> 00:08:53.910
Dr. Clef was still wondering whether that
rascal Dr. Bright was somehow behind this

00:08:53.910 --> 00:08:55.110
fiasco...

00:08:55.110 --> 00:09:00.410
But he was not, because he was actually about
to become MalO’s next victim in its ruthless

00:09:00.410 --> 00:09:02.790
reign of mild to moderate inconvenience.

00:09:02.790 --> 00:09:07.690
Dr. Bright was swanning around the break room
with his favorite morning snack: A coffee

00:09:07.690 --> 00:09:11.570
with extra cream and a danish from his favorite
bakery in town.

00:09:11.570 --> 00:09:15.380
He was looking forward to enjoying these two
simple pleasures in his otherwise incredibly

00:09:15.380 --> 00:09:21.630
stressful life, but little did the poor doctor
know, tragedy was about to strike, and nothing

00:09:21.630 --> 00:09:23.510
would ever be the same.

00:09:23.510 --> 00:09:28.060
Just as the immortal doctor was about to disembark
from the room, MalO appeared right in front

00:09:28.060 --> 00:09:30.620
of him, giving him the mild shock of his life.

00:09:30.620 --> 00:09:35.860
It was such a surprising occurrence, in fact,
that he momentarily lost his grip on his coffee

00:09:35.860 --> 00:09:40.310
mug and his danish, causing both to tumble
to the ground.

00:09:40.310 --> 00:09:42.600
The mug shattered and the danish splattered.

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:47.820
By the time Dr. Bright looked up, MalO was
already gone, just like his breakfast snack.

00:09:47.820 --> 00:09:52.040
Dr. Bright fell to his knees and screamed
“WHHYYYY?”

00:09:52.040 --> 00:09:54.260
up to an indifferent break room ceiling.

00:09:54.260 --> 00:09:57.240
But MalO was just getting started.

00:09:57.240 --> 00:10:02.579
Dr. Kain Pathos Crow was on the way from his
kennel - ahem, we mean, his private quarters

00:10:02.579 --> 00:10:07.290
- to the soul extractor when MalO suddenly
manifested in front of him.

00:10:07.290 --> 00:10:11.680
This resulted in a brief barking match between
the two for dominance over that particular

00:10:11.680 --> 00:10:16.690
hallway, which ended in MalO demanifesting
to bother someone else, which technically

00:10:16.690 --> 00:10:18.610
made Dr. Crow the winner.

00:10:18.610 --> 00:10:22.209
Though Crow himself resented ever being forced
to act like a mere mutt...

00:10:22.209 --> 00:10:28.570
How, he began to wonder, had MalO escaped
its app and begun to harass the real world?

00:10:28.570 --> 00:10:30.990
This would warrant further investigation.

00:10:30.990 --> 00:10:36.680
MalO continued its rampage of irritation across
the site, intending to leave no stone of frustration

00:10:36.680 --> 00:10:37.680
unturned.

00:10:37.680 --> 00:10:41.800
And it wasn’t just the Foundation staff
it intended to freak out; it was just as eager

00:10:41.800 --> 00:10:46.529
to go and bother its fellow anomalies now
it had access to meatspace.

00:10:46.529 --> 00:10:51.890
Yes, that is a real term, we’re not just
being weird and gross, we promise.

00:10:51.890 --> 00:10:56.660
Over in the cell of SCP-173, the Sculpture,
three members of D-Class personnel were cleaning

00:10:56.660 --> 00:10:59.380
up the homicidal creature’s blood and poop.

00:10:59.380 --> 00:11:01.149
They were engaged in the standard procedure.

00:11:01.149 --> 00:11:07.750
One of them mopped, while the other two kept
a close eye on SCP-173 to keep it frozen in

00:11:07.750 --> 00:11:08.750
place.

00:11:08.750 --> 00:11:13.880
That’s when MalO popped into the cell behind
them for a split second before disappearing,

00:11:13.880 --> 00:11:16.660
scaring the living hell out of all three of
them.

00:11:16.660 --> 00:11:22.100
Though the fright was, of course, secondary
to the fact that the second they looked away,

00:11:22.100 --> 00:11:25.030
SCP-173 snapped all three of their necks.

00:11:25.030 --> 00:11:26.030
Oops.

00:11:26.030 --> 00:11:28.860
May have gone a little too far on that one,
eh, MalO?

00:11:28.860 --> 00:11:33.540
But this newly embodied burdensome beast was
just getting started, friends.

00:11:33.540 --> 00:11:36.050
No anomaly was safe from its new antics.

00:11:36.050 --> 00:11:41.740
Next, it appeared in front of SCP-682’s
acid tank, and pulled rude faces at the hateful

00:11:41.740 --> 00:11:44.339
creature from the other side of the glass.

00:11:44.339 --> 00:11:48.589
This only served to sour the creature’s
already utterly horrific mood.

00:11:48.589 --> 00:11:53.329
It thrashed around in the chamber, attempting
to get out and perform an act of great violence,

00:11:53.329 --> 00:12:00.280
but by that time MalO was already long gone,
and SCP-682 was left grumbling in immense

00:12:00.280 --> 00:12:01.500
frustration.

00:12:01.500 --> 00:12:05.670
SCP-049, the Plague Doctor, was having another
very boring day.

00:12:05.670 --> 00:12:10.300
He’d been denied his animal cadaver test
subjects for several days as a disciplinary

00:12:10.300 --> 00:12:15.540
measure after the latest incident, and as
such, he was finding other ways to pass the

00:12:15.540 --> 00:12:16.540
time.

00:12:16.540 --> 00:12:21.449
Today, he was meticulously removing each piece
of medical equipment, polishing them, and

00:12:21.449 --> 00:12:25.279
putting them in a neat line on the desk of
his containment chamber.

00:12:25.279 --> 00:12:28.820
Scalpels, forceps, speculums, bone saws.

00:12:28.820 --> 00:12:31.459
All wonderful, shiny, and pristine.

00:12:31.459 --> 00:12:34.850
The Plague Doctor found it to be an incredibly
calming activity.

00:12:34.850 --> 00:12:39.050
So of course, MalO couldn’t just let him
be.

00:12:39.050 --> 00:12:43.440
The cantankerous canine - driven mad by the
power of suddenly being able to interact with

00:12:43.440 --> 00:12:48.320
the world physically - manifested in the middle
of the containment chamber and used its tail

00:12:48.320 --> 00:12:53.490
to knock all of the meticulously-arranged
medical equipment onto the ground with a thunderous

00:12:53.490 --> 00:12:54.490
clatter.

00:12:54.490 --> 00:12:59.639
The Plague Doctor, devastated, lifted both
hands to his beak and yelled “Sacre Bleu!”

00:12:59.639 --> 00:13:00.639
in horror.

00:13:00.639 --> 00:13:06.990
In that same instant, MalO once again disappeared,
leaving the tragic doctor to start from scratch.

00:13:06.990 --> 00:13:10.329
It was a serious setback on an otherwise lovely
day.

00:13:10.329 --> 00:13:14.370
Curse you, strange dog creature, he thought
to himself while bending over to pick up the

00:13:14.370 --> 00:13:17.260
pieces, curse you and your entire bloodline.

00:13:17.260 --> 00:13:22.440
A group of hardcore Mobile Task Force members
was engaging in the comically manly activity

00:13:22.440 --> 00:13:27.339
of playing poker while smoking in the barracks
- and before you judge them for that, remember

00:13:27.339 --> 00:13:31.510
that if your job was as stressful as being
a member of a Mobile Task Force operative,

00:13:31.510 --> 00:13:33.020
you’d probably smoke too.

00:13:33.020 --> 00:13:38.110
But their job was about to get a little more
stressful when MalO suddenly materialized

00:13:38.110 --> 00:13:43.519
and gave the poker table a sharp kick, sending
the towers of poker chips and deck of cards

00:13:43.519 --> 00:13:47.480
all over the place, before disappearing without
a trace yet again.

00:13:47.480 --> 00:13:49.079
It completely ruined their game.

00:13:49.079 --> 00:13:53.769
One of the more junior members asked, “Should
we have done something about that?”

00:13:53.769 --> 00:13:57.589
A more senior operative shook his head and
said, “We’ll do something when we get

00:13:57.589 --> 00:13:59.480
the official call from the top.

00:13:59.480 --> 00:14:01.759
Until then, let’s reshuffle the deck…”

00:14:01.759 --> 00:14:07.350
In the Site-19 cafeteria, Dr. Agatha Rights
was preparing to eat a delicious salad that

00:14:07.350 --> 00:14:09.790
she’d been waiting all day to enjoy.

00:14:09.790 --> 00:14:14.940
As we’ve often established, working at the
SCP Foundation can be an immensely stressful

00:14:14.940 --> 00:14:20.319
job, so you need to take the small joys where
you can get them, for Dr. Rights, this delicious

00:14:20.319 --> 00:14:25.699
premium salad she bought from Harris Teeter
earlier in the day was indeed a joy.

00:14:25.699 --> 00:14:28.990
She even got a fancy vinaigrette dressing
for the occasion.

00:14:28.990 --> 00:14:33.459
Before she took the first bite, she noticed
SCP-073, Cain, approaching.

00:14:33.459 --> 00:14:36.860
Dr. Rights smiled and gave him a polite nod.

00:14:36.860 --> 00:14:38.480
Cain waved an arm to wave.

00:14:38.480 --> 00:14:41.550
That, our dear viewers, is when tragedy struck.

00:14:41.550 --> 00:14:46.111
MalO suddenly manifested in front of Cain,
propping out one of its canid legs right in

00:14:46.111 --> 00:14:48.970
front of where the hapless anomaly was walking.

00:14:48.970 --> 00:14:53.519
By the time Cain began to trip and fall over,
MalO had already vanished.

00:14:53.519 --> 00:14:54.970
But it was too late.

00:14:54.970 --> 00:14:59.019
Cain kept falling forward until one of his
metal hands landed right into the bowl that

00:14:59.019 --> 00:15:01.339
contained Dr. Rights’ salad.

00:15:01.339 --> 00:15:06.529
Due to his anomalous abilities, the salad
immediately withered away into nasty, dead

00:15:06.529 --> 00:15:07.529
nothingness.

00:15:07.529 --> 00:15:14.190
Dr. Rights began to cry, as Cain, who felt
profoundly guilty, tried his best to apologize.

00:15:14.190 --> 00:15:17.399
Truly nobody in Site-19 was safe.

00:15:17.399 --> 00:15:20.920
MalO popped up behind Iris and ruined all
of her photos.

00:15:20.920 --> 00:15:24.870
MalO popped up behind the Immortal Hitler
Clone in his cell, and gave him a good kick

00:15:24.870 --> 00:15:25.889
in the rear.

00:15:25.889 --> 00:15:31.713
MalO even popped up behind SCP-343, also known
as God, who smugly replied, “I knew you

00:15:31.713 --> 00:15:35.720
were going to do that, my son.”

00:15:35.720 --> 00:15:38.769
Needless to say, it had been one hell of a
day.

00:15:38.769 --> 00:15:43.440
Dr. Segal, completely ignorant to the chaos
his actions had caused around the site, had

00:15:43.440 --> 00:15:46.690
cried in the bathroom for forty minutes out
of sheer disappointment.

00:15:46.690 --> 00:15:50.990
He’d barely been able to focus on the rest
of his duties for the day, on account of being

00:15:50.990 --> 00:15:52.910
severely bummed out.

00:15:52.910 --> 00:15:57.970
This was a day he’d been looking forward
to for so long, and it’d all been for nothing.

00:15:57.970 --> 00:16:03.199
That evening, he was driving home on the highway,
listening to sad songs on the radio, thinking

00:16:03.199 --> 00:16:06.690
about the fact he’d probably just crack
open a beer and get some sleep when he got

00:16:06.690 --> 00:16:07.690
home.

00:16:07.690 --> 00:16:12.399
He sighed again and looked up to adjust his
rearview mirror, when he saw a skeletal face

00:16:12.399 --> 00:16:15.769
with huge, white eyes staring at him in the
reflection.

00:16:15.769 --> 00:16:20.949
A quick, almost reflexive turn revealed that
a huge, black figure with a canine skull for

00:16:20.949 --> 00:16:25.360
a face was indeed just sitting in his back
seat, watching him.

00:16:25.360 --> 00:16:29.750
It was so shocking that he immediately veered
off the road and crashed his car into the

00:16:29.750 --> 00:16:34.920
concrete divider in the middle of the road,
breaking his nose and collarbone in the process.

00:16:34.920 --> 00:16:38.110
Really a perfect cherry on top for this kind
of day.

00:16:38.110 --> 00:16:42.920
Dr. Segal was sitting in the hospital not
long after that, with a cast around his upper

00:16:42.920 --> 00:16:43.920
body.

00:16:43.920 --> 00:16:47.390
This was also where he received a bouquet
of flowers from Dr. Gears, with an attached

00:16:47.390 --> 00:16:53.110
note saying he was put on three-month disciplinary
leave for the irresponsible use of SCP-914.

00:16:53.110 --> 00:16:58.879
Dr. Segal looked up and saw that MalO was
peering around the corner at him with its

00:16:58.879 --> 00:17:04.750
dead, white eyes, its fang-lined maw twisted
into a permanent ominous grin.

00:17:04.750 --> 00:17:10.470
At this point, Dr. Segal realized that being
chased around constantly by a demonic, skull-faced

00:17:10.470 --> 00:17:14.880
anomaly in real life wasn’t nearly as whimsical
as he expected it would be.

00:17:14.880 --> 00:17:19.000
In hindsight, that probably should have been
obvious, shouldn’t it?

00:17:19.000 --> 00:17:23.230
Though please, let us know if you’d like
MalO to stalk you in real life in the comments

00:17:23.230 --> 00:17:25.810
below, you bunch of weirdos...

00:17:25.810 --> 00:17:33.289
Now go check out “SCP-1471 - Mal0 Version
1.0.0” and “SCP-914 What Did YOU Put In

00:17:33.289 --> 00:17:36.320
It!?” for more on today’s unique and strange
anomalies!

